From a95d099122a2bec944ab36cfcc87d6cd7aa781a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dhruvgupta-zetesis <dhruv@zetesislabs.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 04:57:48 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Fix the kernel-environment lookup, complete the v4.31
 primitive list, and pin each test's reason

The quotient post-check looked constants up with Lean.Environment.find?, which on an
environment rebuilt from a kernel environment sees only imported constants; it now asks the
kernel environment. eagerReduce, Lean.reduceBool, Lean.reduceNat and Bool join the primitives
(the v4.31 kernel names them). The test runner now also checks that the output names the
expected reason, and the three prelude tests that exited early because their exports were
incomplete now reach the check they exercise.
